    {
      "v": 9,
      "zh": "这都是为以色列众人和在他们中间寄居的外人所分定的城邑，使误杀人的都可以逃到那里，不死在报血仇人的手中，等他站在会众面前听审判。",
      "en": "These were the cities of refuge[NOTE:1] appointed for all the Israelites and for resident foreigners living among them. Anyone who accidentally killed someone could escape there and not be executed by[NOTE:2] the avenger of blood, at least until his case was reviewed by the assembly.[NOTE:3]",
      "notes": [
        "The Hebrew text reads simply “the cities.” The words “for refuge” are supplied for clarification.",
        "Heb “and not die by the hand of.”",
        "Heb “until he stands before the assembly.” The words “at least” are supplied for clarification."
